<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/4/eng@/~part_IV__cl_32__subsec_2> <https://schema.org/text> "When in any proceedings for an offence under this Act it is necessary to prove that any person was, or was not, the holder of a licence, a certificate purporting to be signed by the Commissioner and certifying that a person was or was not, the holder of a licence, shall be admissible as evidence and shall constitute prima facie proof of the facts certified in such certificate, without proof of the signature of the Commissioner to such certificate. Presumptions"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/4/eng@> .
